{title: 443 - There'll Be No Sorrow There}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #443 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 443}
{meta: category Early Advent - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]There'll be no [C]night in heaven,
[F]In that blest [C]world above;
[C7]No anxious toil, [Bb]no weary [F]hours;
[F/A]For labor [C]there is love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]There'll be no sorrow [C]there,
[C]There'll be no [F]sorrow [C]there;
[C7]In heaven above, [Bb]where all is [F]love,
[F/A]There'll be [C]no sorrow there.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]There'll be no [C]grief in heaven;
[F]For life is [C]one glad day,
[C7]And tears [F]are [C7]those [Bb]of former [F]things
[F/A]Which all [C]have passed away.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]There'll be no [C]sin in heaven;
[F]Behold [C]that blessed throng,
[C7]All holy in there [Bb]spotless robes,
[F/A]All holy [C]in their song.
{end_of_verse}
